; How writes are brought into their constraints: unit is clamped to 0 to 1, n is rounded to an
; int, way holds its last valid choice, and pos skips a write that breaks (> 0). The runtime
; tests make the writes; the table shows the starting values.

(type side string (one-of 'left' 'right'))
(real unit 0.5 (>= 0) (<= 1))
(int n 0)
(side way 'left')
(real pos 1 (> 0))
